    "description": "Advanced to staff software engineer role and led development of TurboTax’s cross-platform  C++ core technology and associated content development tools, comprised of 1.5 million lines of code running on Windows, Mac/iPad, Linux, and Sun.\n\nWrote application used to create core data model to prepare federal, state, and city tax returns; tool used to create form images, fields, and additional attributes per each defined TurboTax product.\n\nPlayed key role as senior member of team responsible for maintaining and enhancing large cross-platform C++ forms and calculation engine used to create and execute core content for Turbo Tax and other Intuit products; clients included content developers, software engineers, and quality engineers across diverse business units.\n\nLed product innovation, creating and implementing domain-specific language that allowed content developers to convert data from Intuit’s proprietary tax return format into IRS’s MEF format for electronic filing.",
